codemap 9
tour feature-comment
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note The human reading the map in a terminal beside the agent, with 'codemap . tour <name>' or 'show' instead of the window, at the moment a step or lines raise a question. Goal: the map is the second channel beside the source, read in the CLI as much as in the GUI. Without this command the CLI reader, who sees every step's index in brackets and its file:lines in the 'tour' output, had no way to leave the question the window's buttons leave, and had to retype the place into the chat like the GUI reader before add-comment; the Console, which runs every other command, had the same gap. In the CLI the place is printed text the human can copy, which is what the GUI's Source view lacks. It resolves the place the way tour-add does (a tour name, a step index, a file and 1-based inclusive lines anchored to the enclosing symbol), refuses an unknown tour, step, file or range and an empty text, and writes through the same store as add-comment, authored by whoever runs it. The CLI scenario 'comments' runs each outcome. Why comments exist and the designs that were tried are in feature-add-comment.

